// "GainsLife" = a player gained life ([CR#119.3]: an effect causing a
// player to gain life adjusts their life total accordingly). Mirrors
// event/Attacks + event/Dies (single Predicate-typed subject slot); the
// subject is a PLAYER identity, not an object, so it's parsed by
// `filter::recipient_phrase` (the "you"/"an opponent"/"a player" grammar),
// not `filter::parse_phrase` — there's no `~` self shorthand, since a
// permanent is never "you".
// Usage: GainsLife(who) — e.g. GainsLife(Ref(You)), GainsLife(OpponentOf(Ref(You))).
(
    name: "GainsLife",
    template: "${0} gain life",
    kinds: [EventFilter],
    params: [Predicate],
    body: LifeGained(who: Param(0)),
)
